OL,3,GNEWSAThe teenage killer who talked his
OL,4,Away into the noose
OL,5,
OL,6,FHerbert Leonard Mills stated "I am
OL,7,Fquite proud of my achievement" as he
OL,8,Fconfessed to murdering housewife Mabel
OL,9,FTattershaw.
OL,11,FThe 19-year-old had not made the
OL,12,Fadmission to the police, rather News of
OL,13,Fthe World reporter Norman Rae in the
OL,14,Flobby of a hotel in Nottingham on 25
OL,15,FAugust 1951.
OL,17,FRae promptly marched Mills to a police
OL,18,Fstation. He was convicted of murder
OL,19,Fafter a trial and was hanged at Lincoln
OL,20,FPrison just months after the killing.
